{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make `_git_subcommand` treat all separate-token valued git global options (`--git-dir`, `--work-tree`, `--namespace`, `--super-prefix`) as two-token skips, or document it only handles `-c`/`-C`.","criteria":["correctness","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py:84: `if argv[i] in (\"-c\", \"-C\"):`","tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py:86: `elif argv[i].startswith(\"-\"):` then `i += 1` — treats `--git-dir`/`--work-tree` as flags with no value","ABSENCE: the current commit argvs only use `-C`/`-c` so the helper is correct for this test, but it is written as a general git-argv parser and would misread other valued options"],"finding":"`_git_subcommand` only special-cases `-c`/`-C` as two-token options; any other valued global option that takes a SEPARATE-token argument (`--git-dir <path>`, `--work-tree <path>`, `--namespace <x>`) is skipped as a single token, so its following value is misidentified as the git subcommand. This can misclassify a process (e.g. tag a non-commit as a commit sid, or mask a real `repack` subcommand).","id":"0","impact":0.0,"location":"tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py:80","norm_id":"n489002528354f4cb","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable